<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Strategy factory, one cycle per day (issue #38). Full rationale in ops/README.md:
  why 17:00 (an hour before the 18:00 run, so a promotion opens its book the same
  evening), why this job calls a bare script instead of the tradefabe console script,
  and why PYTHONPATH is baked in.

  Two traps this file already fell into, both of which fail as EX_CONFIG (78) with an
  empty log, so there is nothing to read that tells you why:

  1. Logs must NOT live under the repo. It sits in ~/Documents, which is TCC-protected,
     and the Homebrew python this job execs cannot write there under launchd. The two
     older jobs get away with state/logs/ because they exec the tradefabe console
     script, which was granted access; a fresh binary is not. Hence ~/Library/Logs.
  2. Keep this comment free of doubled hyphens. XML forbids them inside comments, and
     plutil lint accepts them anyway while stricter parsers reject the file. Check with
     xmllint, not plutil.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>com.dzheng.tradefabe.factory</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/Users/dzheng/Documents/tradefabe/.venv/bin/python</string>
    <string>/Users/dzheng/Documents/tradefabe/research/factory_run.py</string>
    <string>--n</string>
    <string>20</string>
  </array>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key><string>/Users/dzheng/Documents/tradefabe</string>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PYTHONPATH</key>
    <string>/Users/dzheng/Documents/tradefabe/src:/Users/dzheng/Documents/tradefabe:/Users/dzheng/Documents/tradefabe/research</string>
  </dict>
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>17</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>0</integer></dict>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>/Users/dzheng/Library/Logs/tradefabe/factory.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/Users/dzheng/Library/Logs/tradefabe/factory.err</string>
</dict>
</plist>
